---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';

/**
 * Privacy (T2.3). Scoped to what this site actually does today, verified
 * against the build rather than written from a template:
 *
 *   * waitlist   — WaitlistForm POSTs email + `tag` fields straight to
 *                  Buttondown (docs/waitlist.md); nothing of ours sits between.
 *   * hosting    — Vercel (DEPLOYMENT.md), which logs requests.
 *   * fonts      — Google Fonts, loaded cross-origin by Base.astro.
 *   * storage    — one localStorage key, `tt-theme` (theme-init.js). No cookies.
 *   * analytics  — none.
 *
 * If any of those changes — an analytics script, a new form, a new processor —
 * this page changes in the same commit, and `updated` moves with it.
 */
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  updated="2026-10-15"
  description="What the Tamtree website collects, why, who processes it, and how to have it deleted. No analytics, no advertising, no tracking cookies."
>
  <p class="legal__lead">
    This website collects as little as it can: the email address you give us if you join the
    waitlist, and the request data any web host sees. There are no analytics, no advertising and
    no tracking cookies.
  </p>

  <p>
    This policy covers <strong>www.tamtree.io</strong> and its waitlist. It does not cover the
    Tamtree product itself, which will have its own terms and privacy policy when it launches.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    This site is operated by Tamtree (“we”, “us”). For anything in this policy, write
    to <a href="mailto:hello@tamtree.io">hello@tamtree.io</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>

  <h3>If you join the waitlist</h3>
  <p>
    We collect your <strong>email address</strong> and the options you tick (for example “launch
    news” or “early-access beta”). We use them only to email you about Tamtree’s launch and early
    access. Your browser sends the form directly to our email provider, Buttondown, which stores the
    list on our behalf; the address never passes through a server of ours.
  </p>
  <p>
    We rely on your <strong>consent</strong> to do this. You can withdraw it at any time with the
    unsubscribe link in any email we send, or by writing to us.
  </p>

  <h3>When you visit any page</h3>
  <p>
    Our host, Vercel, receives the information every web request carries — your IP address,
    browser and device details, the page requested and the time — in order to deliver the page and
    protect the site from abuse. We do not use this data to identify you or to build a profile.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our pages load their typefaces from <strong>Google Fonts</strong>, so your browser also
    connects to Google’s servers, which receive your IP address and browser details as part of that
    request.
  </p>

  <h3>Stored on your device</h3>
  <p>
    If you switch between light and dark mode, your choice is saved in your browser’s local storage
    under the key <code>tt-theme</code>. It never leaves your device and you can clear it at any
    time. We set no cookies.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not run analytics or tracking scripts.</li>
    <li>We do not show advertising or use advertising pixels.</li>
    <li>We do not sell, rent or trade personal data.</li>
    <li>We do not use your data to train AI models.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who processes data for us</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Buttondown</strong> — stores and sends email for the waitlist.</li>
    <li><strong>Vercel</strong> — hosts and delivers this website.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong> — serves the typefaces the pages use.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These providers may process data in the United States and other countries outside your own.
    Where the law requires it, those transfers rely on the providers’ standard contractual
    safeguards.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep your waitlist email until you unsubscribe, ask us to delete it, or we close the
    waitlist — whichever comes first. Request logs are kept by Vercel for the short period its
    service requires, and are not otherwise retained by us.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access the personal data we hold about
    you, to correct it, to have it deleted, to object to or restrict how it is used, and to receive
    a copy of it. Email <a href="mailto:hello@tamtree.io">hello@tamtree.io</a> and we will act on
    your request promptly and within the time the law allows. You also have the right to complain
    to your local data protection authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site is meant for professionals and is not directed at children under 16. We do not
    knowingly collect their data; if you believe a child has joined the waitlist, tell us and we
    will delete the address.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If what we collect or how we use it changes, we will update this page and the date at the top.
    If you are on the waitlist and the change is significant, we will tell you by email before it
    takes effect.
  </p>
</Legal>
